ROW 20 §4.7 review recency attested (hard rule)
docs/phase-0-prereg.md:564: ### 4.7 Review recency is itself attested (hard rule)
docs/phase-0-prereg.md:565: This pre-registration's exit gate (§5) uses **multi-model adversarial review** —
docs/phase-0-prereg.md:566: not a professional human audit, and not claimed as one. A substantive human
docs/phase-0-prereg.md:567: audit requires a paid expert; anything less labelled "audit" would be theater. A
docs/phase-0-prereg.md:568: real system has a *recurring* review cycle, not a one-time blessing. So review
docs/phase-0-prereg.md:569: recency is made a verifiable property: the service attests *when it was last
docs/phase-0-prereg.md:570: adversarially reviewed* (signed, timestamped), and review staleness beyond a
docs/phase-0-prereg.md:571: declared threshold fails the invariant. The system that attests artifacts
docs/phase-0-prereg.md:572: attests its own audit recency — dogfooding, not decoration.

