   210	
   211	## A3.3 The symbolic suite and the capstone gate
   212	
   213	**Registered obligation (requirement level; ruled in dialogue
   214	2026-07-28, restated and adopted 2026-08-07, commit 68b581c):**
   215	per-property ProVerif models over a shared theory library; every model
   216	carries an explicit assumes-from-elsewhere ledger holding **two entry
   217	kinds** — dischargeable cross-model obligations, and exposed Layer 2
   218	assumptions.
   219	
   220	> Band 0 exit is gated on a capstone composition context in which
   221	> every ledgered **cross-model** assumption — a fact one symbolic
   222	> model assumes and another must establish — is discharged by a
   223	> machine-checked producer query and carries a broken companion that
   224	> **fails the query consuming the severed link**. Layer 2 assumptions
   225	> (cryptographic primitive security, historical trust-anchor
   226	> correctness, chain availability, implementation fidelity,
   227	> operational independence of authority channels) are explicitly
   228	> exposed and unclaimed in the ledger — never discharged, never
   229	> silently absorbed. Any termination-forced scoping is named in-module
   230	> and disposed by amendment discipline, never silently.
   231	
   232	**Ledger conservation rule** (each entry records at least): consumer
   233	property/query; assumed fact; producer module and event/query (or
   234	"Layer 2 — unclaimed"); the shared term establishing correspondence;
   235	adversary capabilities at the join; and any residual Layer 2
   236	assumption. A cross-model entry additionally records the broken
   237	mutation and expected failing query; those fields do not pretend to
   238	discharge a Layer 2 entry.
   239	
   240	**The mechanism spike precedes the suite scaffold** (design adopted
   241	2026-08-07): representative complexity first — the §A3.2 witness
   242	chain, the structural worst case — ablating toward the break point on
   243	failure; the drafted ledger interface is the spike's scaffolding (one
   244	artifact); per-query timebox declared before running with three named
   245	outcomes (query violation = counterexample; timeout = mechanism
   246	failure, not property evidence; termination = evidence for the checked
   247	abstraction only); predictions registered before running. The
   248	transcription-pattern capstone is a non-binding implementation
   249	candidate, subject to the spike.
   250	
   251	**Additional model obligations from this amendment:** the capstone's
   252	linkage query proves the §A3.2 chain (the links, not just
   253	cardinalities, per-layer); the P4 model's unknown-algorithm transition
   254	(§A3.6) carries its own companion; every symbolic lemma carries a
   255	prose mapping to its registered property (standing rule, reaffirmed).
