   834	## A3.10 What changed, and what did not
   835	
   836	**Tightenings (strengthen, never weaken):** the A1.2.1 waiver lattice
   837	gains the linked floor (§A3.2) — every prior `VALID_DEGRADED` verdict
   838	that satisfied the floors still verifies; verdicts that satisfied
   839	counted-but-unlinked evidence never had a registered guarantee to
   840	lose. The H0 headline is corrected to its operative form (§A3.1.2),
   841	which is the form the models check. The unknown-algorithm verdict
   842	boundary (§A3.6.2) instantiates the existing P4 partition; it adds no
   843	states.
   844	
   845	**Additions:** survivability claims and layered bundle contents
   846	(§A3.4), tending and rotation obligations (§A3.5), agility
   847	obligations (§A3.6), residue closures and orthogonal standing
   848	assessment (§A3.7), structured assessment scope and optional report
   849	attestation (§A3.8). Additions impose new obligations on Tessera, none
   850	on prior artifacts.
   851	
   852	**The A2.3 completion, named (it changes the obligation's apparent
   853	owner):** A2.3 registered refusal durability, retrievability, and
   854	reporting without assigning their bearer; §A3.7.2 assigns them — to
   855	the generating authority until verified handoff, to the declared
   856	custodian after it, with the published commitment — once externally
   857	acknowledged — becoming the surviving public trace — and names one
   858	honest impossibility (the pre-handoff death interval)
   859	rather than registering a claim no architecture can keep. No A2.3
   860	obligation weakens: refusal remains atomic, latching, and
   861	first-class; what changes is that its evidence now has named
   862	custodians and visible failure states where the registered text had a
   863	passive voice.
   864	
   865	**Explicitly not changed:** P4's verdict partition (it becomes one
   866	component of the larger assessment, not the whole result model); P9
   867	statelessness (tending state never enters a bundle verdict); A2.1's
   868	clock roles (tending triggers get their own eventual mechanism and
   869	trust assumptions); the A2.4 standing rules; the misissuance boundary
   870	(A1.3.7).
   871	
   872	**The A1.1 falsifier is not triggered:** no property is weakened; no
   873	discharge is abandoned; the scoping honesty of the capstone gate
   874	(cross-model discharged, Layer 2 exposed) narrows a gate ruled in
   875	dialogue to what a symbolic prover can honestly discharge, and was
   876	adopted in that form before this draft existed (commit `68b581c`).
