226:**R-2.1** The issuer signs with two keys from independent failure domains — KMS for cloud-native custody, local GPG counter-signing for a portable independent WHO layer — both over the same canonical bytes. [REGISTERED prereg §3.1 "Decision: C.", docs/phase-0-prereg.md:273-298]
244:### 2.2 Authority channels
246:**R-2.10** The issuer-key manifest carries two independent, archived, time-anchored authority-publication evidences — the DNSSEC chain snapshot and the anchored repository publication — plus a manifest self-signature by the issuer keys. [REGISTERED A1 P10 / §A1.5, docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-1.md:283-297, 430-442]
