   264	**Issuance window.** The key-publication record carries `issuance-not-before` (optional) and `issuance-not-after`
   265	(mandatory), identical in DNS and the git blob (ENCODING-V1 §7, §7.1, D-17). A receipt is `INVALID /
   266	ISSUANCE_WINDOW` unless not-before ≤ `declared_issue_time` and T ≤ not-after, with T as registered and no margin.
   267	*Operating parameters* (not verifier rules): **30-day windows**, overlapping so a successor key is published before
   268	its predecessor retires; the issuer **stops signing with a key 96 h before its not-after** (δ = 72 h, the longest registered gap from
   269	signing to anchor, plus 24 h for header-time skew; OWNER DECISION 2026-10-12, replacing an earlier 48 h figure that
   270	was shorter than δ); the repository key is an
   271	offline hardware root used only for rotations. An attempt whose T would fall after not-after is incomplete, is not
   272	shipped, and is reissued under the successor key.
