    48	
    49	## A1.0 Why amend before starting
    50	
    51	The review found that the pre-registration, as signed, could be *passed by a
    52	proof that does not protect the project*. H0 pre-registered that a
    53	machine-checked proof would exist, but not **what it must prove**. That gap
    54	is precisely the drift-vector formal-methods theater needs: months into the
    55	modeling, the provable-in-practice properties drift toward whatever the
    56	model makes easy, and "the proof holds" quietly becomes "the proof of
    57	whatever we managed to prove holds." The agreement gate, as written, would
    58	judge fidelity only *after* any such drift, by the same parties who drifted.
    59	
    60	This amendment closes that gap by pre-registering the property list
    61	(A1.2), the degraded-policy semantics (A1.2.1), the adversary model (A1.3),
    62	and the tooling rationale and choice discipline (A1.4). It also resolves
    63	one design hole the review surfaced (manifest authority, A1.5), states the
    64	temporal-anchor semantics precisely (A1.6), and hardens the agreement gate
    65	from a confirmation task into a falsification task (A1.7). The original
    66	objectives, bands, and invariants are not weakened; this amendment *adds*
    67	resolution and evidence obligations (A1.8).
    68	
    69	---
    70	
    71	## A1.1 Clarification of the H0 falsifier
    72	
    73	The original's phrasing — "if the guarantee cannot be proven, there is
    74	nothing worth building" — could be misread as one-shot: first failed proof
    75	attempt, project over. That is not the claim and never was. The method is
    76	iterative, as all modeling is: model, attempt proof, find the flaw, revise,
    77	re-prove — with each revision recorded in the journal.
    78	
    79	Iteration within scope is ordinary work. **Falsification is scope
    80	reduction.** Precisely: H0 (as amended) is falsified if any A1.2 property
    81	cannot be discharged without one of the following:
    82	
    83	- **weakening the property** as pre-registered;
    84	- **demoting** a property from `[model]`/`[proof]` to `[assumption]`;
    85	- **excluding** a declared A1.3 adversary capability;
    86	- **changing the construction so materially** that it no longer implements
    87	  the dual-signature + temporal-anchor design of §3.1.
    88	
    89	Any such weakening requires a further signed, dated amendment stating what
    90	was weakened and why; absent that amendment, Phase 1 does not begin. This
    91	gives a future reader a concrete way to see whether Band 0 succeeded,
    92	failed, or changed scope — rather than an unfalsifiable "no model could be
    93	built." Building the service on a foundation that required concealed
    94	weakening would be theater; that, and only that, is what the original
    95	sentence forbids.
    96	
