    37	## A4.1 P9 and P10: tool assignment and discharge path
    38	
    39	**What Amendment 1 says.** §A1.4 assigns P9 and P10 to TLA+ among the
    40	state-machine properties. §A1.2 marks both **[model]**. No TLA+ model
    41	of either exists, and none was scheduled.
    42	
    43	**P10 — amended tool assignment: ProVerif.** P10's registered property
    44	sentence — *an adversary controlling any proper subset of the external
    45	authority channels cannot cause a manifest asserting a non-authorized
    46	key to satisfy the `VALID_STRICT` evidence requirement* — is exactly
    47	what the first-link spike's Q1 and Q3 proved in both leaked-channel
    48	variants (`formal/spike/first-link/`, decision `459aff0`) and what
    49	S-P3's strict-mode Q1 proved again under the shared library
    50	(`formal/suite/s-p3/`). The A1.4 assignment predates the tool
    51	decision; the symbolic verifier is the right tool for an adversary
    52	claim. P10's **[model]** half is discharged by those runs, at the
    53	`checked` level, on this amendment's signature; its degraded half
    54	("names which authority evidence was waived and why") is P4's
    55	explicit-policy logic and is carried there. The possession half
    56	(manifest self-signature, A1.5 item 3) is S-P3 ledger entry 2,
    57	already labelled as P10-carried-in-S-P3.
    58	
    59	**P9 — amended discharge: inspection plus conformance vector.** A TLA+
    60	model of "the verdict is a pure function of bundle and policy" would
    61	be stateless because its author wrote it stateless — the
    62	companion-that-cannot-fail pattern this record already names as
    63	theater. P9 is discharged by (i) an enumeration of the reference
    64	verifier's inputs, which the standing probe's Q6 produced
    65	(`formal/spike/standing-probe/RESULTS-PROBE.md`), carried into the
    66	coverage map and re-checked against the reference verifier at H1a; and
    67	(ii) one H1a red-bar vector: the same bundle and declared policy,
    68	verified on two isolated machines with no network, must yield the same
    69	verdict, and a verifier that consults any optional service must fail
    70	the vector. P9's discharge label changes from **[model]** to
    71	**[inspection + vector]**.
    72	
    73	**Optional TLA+ probes, non-discharging — RULED (author).** The author
    74	asked what is lost by not building the TLA+ models and ruled that they
    75	be built anyway as *probes* in the design-probe tier (ruling of
    76	2026-08-29): *"If they don't find anything, we don't use it as
    77	evidence. If they do find something, we can act upon that between now
    78	and exit."* So: the collaborator builds TLA+ models of P9 and P10 on
    79	its own schedule; a green result is **not evidence** and is not cited
    80	by any tracker row; a red result or an unrepresentable-attack finding
