   156	## A5.4 P2: all required signers attest to the same content — ADOPTED (author)
   157	
   158	**What the review found** (cross-family review item 12; S-P2
   159	`sp2_q2_degraded_compromised.pv`). Two honest signers under one
   160	manifest can sign *different* payloads and the verifier accepts. P2's
   161	registered text says the signed bytes commit to the required-signer
   162	manifest and never says the signers attest to common content; the
   163	frozen plan assumed it.
   164	
   165	**The framing fork** (Codex pre-read, 2026-09-11). Each signer's
   166	frame carries that signer's own key fingerprint inside the signed
   167	bytes (P3's field list), so two signers' frames can never be
   168	byte-equal. Either (a) common attested content in separate,
   169	signer-specific frames, or (b) one shared frame with the key binding
   170	moved into the manifest — which changes P3's field list and P8's
   171	frame layout for multi-signer objects.
   172	
   173	**Registered: (a).** The author: *"C8 seems obvious to me - what does
   174	it mean if they signed different bytes?"* **How that is read, stated
   175	so it can be corrected** (the wording is ROUTED's, not a stronger
   176	one): the author's sentence endorses C8's recommendation, which is
   177	(a); he did not name (a) or (b) himself. If he meant (b) — one shared
   178	frame — then P3's field list and P8's frame change and the S-P2
   179	addendum registered below is withdrawn. For a multi-signer
