   242	- *Dispatch and aggregation.* As in the profile: out-of-profile at dispatch, A4.2 precedence inside it. An unsupported request over an intact bundle is distinguished from a fresh strict request.
   243	- *H1a's suite.* Forge, tamper, backdate, break-chain (retained chains), strip-one-signature, out-of-profile, and the A9.1 mapping. Degradation and wrapper instances move to their capabilities.
   244	- *Future compatibility.* A later wrapper must preserve the inner V1 assessment under identical declared inputs and report its outer and LTV assessments separately. This is a future obligation, not something already checked.
   245	- *Custody.* V1 offers no renewal. Long-horizon validity depends on the dependency manifest's algorithms (including SHA-1 in git object linkage) and on the holder keeping the bundle. Independent custodians may later renew under another profile.
