   595	target is resolvable either (i) from material inside the bundle or (ii) from an input the verifier's
   596	declared policy explicitly names as trusted (the §2.3 trust configuration) — and never by a live
   597	lookup. Under (ii) the reference stays inside P9's pure function, the declared policy being one of
   598	its two arguments. A reference the verifier can resolve from neither makes the check that needs it
   599	unperformable: `UNVERIFIABLE` for that required check, under the P4 partition. A1 §A1.5's "archived
